          "source_text_sha256": "5acadc9d2babc6cc0b2a681ec1a9a0ff1789f574f003d305b3898d9f70c7a9c7",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 9, 2015, around 7 PM, two witnesses in the department of Seine-et-Marne (77) observed the rapid passage of a luminous phenomenon in the sky. The phenomenon is described as a glowing ball with a tail. This observation, lasting a few seconds, of a glowing ball followed by a tail is typical of a meteoroid atmospheric reentry phenomenon. See the article \"Is it a Meteor?\" The GEIPAN received another simultaneous observation report and the specialized site IMO (International Meteor Organization) received 14. (see on the IMO site). Therefore, the GEIPAN classifies this case as A: certain observations of a meteoroid atmospheric reentry that caused a meteor.",
